<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 22.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 22.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 11/22/96  11/15/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    208.67    215.72    89.73	92.76     87.90</p>
<p>West	    216.65    225.17    81.81	85.02     75.90</p>
<p>Total Canada  425.33    440.89    85.51	88.64     81.60</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 11/22/96: 232.55 bcf, 11/15/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 11/22/96: 264.84 bcf, 11/15/96: 264.84 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
